From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] The navigation bar gets its own key: one tap puts it away

The reader asked to own the bar's visibility. This patch gives the bar one more key at the
right-hand end, next to Recents: a chevron pointing down onto a line. A tap toggles the bar
-- patch 0076 owns the state, applies it, and puts the bar back on a swipe up from the
bottom edge.

The nav bar's layout is a string from SystemUI's own resources -- `config_navBarLayout` in
`packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml` -- and its keys are inflated from it by
`NavigationBarInflaterView`, so this is a new token (`navlock`) and a new layout for it, not
a change to framework-res: no resource ID that the ART boot image depends on moves. The
button is a plain `ImageView` rather than a `KeyButtonView`, because it sends no key code.

The key does not touch Settings itself: it sends the broadcast introduced by patch 0076 and
the policy side owns the state, so there is one place that decides.

Not run on a device yet when this patch was written; how to run it is in
`readom-port/reports/t09-nav-impl.md`.

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml b/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml
--- a/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/res/values/config.xml
@@ -339,7 +339,8 @@
     <bool name="config_quickSettingsOnFirstPull">false</bool>
 
     <!-- Nav bar button default ordering/layout -->
-    <string name="config_navBarLayout" translatable="false">left[.5W],back[1WC];home;recent[1WC],right[.5W]</string>
+    <!-- Readom: navlock is the bar's own key (readom_nav_key.xml). -->
+    <string name="config_navBarLayout" translatable="false">left[.5W],back[1WC];home;recent[1WC],navlock[1WC],right[.5W]</string>
 
     <bool name="quick_settings_show_full_alarm">false</bool>
 
